# Local environment for this agent. Copy to `.secrets/.env` (git-ignored, never shipped in builds or
# container images) and uncomment what you need. Everything here is OPTIONAL — defaults work without a .env.

# --- Model auth ---
# Pick auth once: `fastagent login` (an account such as ChatGPT for openai, or an API key),
# or set a provider API key here — the variable name is provider-specific (e.g. OPENAI_API_KEY,
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY). `fastagent dev` then lets you choose a model from whatever you're logged into.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Model selection (overrides fastagent.config.ts) ---
# Precedence: --model flag > FASTAGENT_MODEL > config. Local commands (`dev`, `start`, `invoke`, `info`,
# `login`) read this file; containers get their values from the host environment instead. To set the default
# model everywhere, configure `model` in fastagent.config.ts.
# FASTAGENT_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.5

# --- Serving & HTTP Agent API ---
# Set FASTAGENT_API_KEY to enable the Agent API under /v1 (`Authorization: Bearer <key>`).
# FASTAGENT_API_KEY=
# Port precedence: --port > PORT > 8787 (`start`)
# PORT=8787
# Instance root: the agent's working directory, with durable state under .state/.
# Default: <agent dir>/.fastagent/<dev|start>. Point it at a mounted volume in deployments.
# FASTAGENT_ROOT=/data
